{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134087-investigations-clarification-contradiction","id":1134087,"title":"Investigations - Clarification & Contradiction","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-26T02:10:58-07:00","id":1134087,"title":"Investigations - Clarification & Contradiction","content":"Been looking into the Investigations mechanics and I really like how it seems to encourage the players taking part in shaping the story. But I am a little confused since later on in the book they seem to discard that aspect.<br /> <br /> p. 78, at the top: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;When they succeed, ask them, \u201cWhat do you find?\u201d and let their answers inform the direction of your story.&quot; </div> </div> </div>p. 79, under Step Two: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Once the characters go digging for Clues, you have to determine what they find and what it means. Ask some simple questions of the player. \u201cWhere is she searching?\u201d \u201cWhat does she hope to uncover here?\u201d \u201cHow does she think he did it?\u201d </div> </div> </div>So the second quotation seems to follow the &quot;old way&quot; of playing rather than let the players shape the Clues they find.<br /> <br /> So, I am kinda hoping for a better example of the &quot;freeform&quot; way of using this, since I think the examples in Step Two is an error (doesn't follow the rest of the mechanics description by allowing the players to determine the Clues).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T06:04:58-07:00","id":1134122,"title":"","content":"I would treat letting the players have a say as optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T07:15:50-07:00","id":1134133,"title":"","content":"Depends on how much time you have.<br /> <br /> Since it is a mystery, no one (but you) knows how it is going to play out. So when you haven't actually constructed anything yet, you can have Players' guesses build it out for you. Simply decide if they are right, wrong, or close (advise making it a mix of the 3), and work out the plot from there. They have no way of knowing it wasn't what you intended all along. And it has the bonus of being believable to them (they thought of it, after all).<br /> <br /> You could also mix in a few static points, then let player suggestions flesh out the details.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T07:16:16-07:00","id":1134134,"title":"","content":"I think &quot;what do you find?&quot; would be better read as &quot;what <i>sort of thing</i> do find?&quot; Like, I wouldn't let the player say &quot;I find the killer's footprints&quot; because the players have no way of knowing that's even a possible thing to find. This beIng CofD, the killer might have some supernatural means of concealing their footprints, or might not even have feet for all the players know. Instead, I would accept the player saying &quot;I find something that would indicate where the killer went next&quot;. Then I would determine what exactly the player finds that would satisfy their criteria. Maybe it ends up being footprints, maybe it ends up being a trail of ectoplasm, maybe it ends up being a businesses card that fell out of the killer's pocket, as long as it's something that points the players in the direction of where the killer went next.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T12:30:14-07:00","id":1134220,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4714\" data-vbnamecard=\"4714\">Live Bait</a> <br /> I can also imagene that having it as optional would work better. Unless you truelly wanted to run a setting with no planned out outcome before hand. However, it would still need a kicker.. Like a dead body, an odd passenger, mystical castle, etc..<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> <br /> So by static points, you mean have already made &quot;scenes&quot; where the players can find an shape the Clues?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134087-investigations-clarification-contradiction?p=1134134#post1134134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;what do you find?&quot; would be better read as &quot;what <i>sort of thing</i> do find?&quot; Like, I wouldn't let the player say &quot;I find the killer's footprints&quot; because the players have no way of knowing that's even a possible thing to find. This beIng CofD, the killer might have some supernatural means of concealing their footprints, or might not even have feet for all the players know. Instead, I would accept the player saying &quot;I find something that would indicate where the killer went next&quot;. Then I would determine what exactly the player finds that would satisfy their criteria. Maybe it ends up being footprints, maybe it ends up being a trail of ectoplasm, maybe it ends up being a businesses card that fell out of the killer's pocket, as long as it's something that points the players in the direction of where the killer went next.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually also bring up another problem I had: How do I guide my players in using it.<br /> <br /> I can imagen to some that being in that much charge can be overwhelming.. Or become a sort of power trip..<br /> <br /> ==============================<br /> <br /> ... I really would have liked the book to actually have some proper examples on how to do this -_-'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T12:37:38-07:00","id":1134223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134087-investigations-clarification-contradiction?p=1134220#post1134220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a> <br /> So by static points, you mean have already made &quot;scenes&quot; where the players can find an shape the Clues?</div> </div> </div> </div>Static bits like Person A was killed. Person B did it. Person C ordered it. Why, where, how, and who else is involved can be filled out via guesses. Or maybe the how or why is static, with who being determined later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:42:10-07:00","id":1134261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134087-investigations-clarification-contradiction?p=1134134#post1134134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think &quot;what do you find?&quot; would be better read as &quot;what <i>sort of thing</i> do find?&quot; Like, I wouldn't let the player say &quot;I find the killer's footprints&quot; because the players have no way of knowing that's even a possible thing to find. This beIng CofD, the killer might have some supernatural means of concealing their footprints, or might not even have feet for all the players know. Instead, I would accept the player saying &quot;I find something that would indicate where the killer went next&quot;. Then I would determine what exactly the player finds that would satisfy their criteria. Maybe it ends up being footprints, maybe it ends up being a trail of ectoplasm, maybe it ends up being a businesses card that fell out of the killer's pocket, as long as it's something that points the players in the direction of where the killer went next.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That would work great in some kind of a system where at end of the investigations, players accrue a certain number of Clue Points and then can trade them in to unlock options from a list provided by a GM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:43:23-07:00","id":1134262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134087-investigations-clarification-contradiction?p=1134220#post1134220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4714\" data-vbnamecard=\"4714\">Live Bait</a><br /> I can also imagene that having it as optional would work better. Unless you truelly wanted to run a setting with no planned out outcome before hand. However, it would still need a kicker.. Like a dead body, an odd passenger, mystical castle, etc..<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7212_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7212\" data-vbnamecard=\"7212\">Vent0</a><br /> So by static points, you mean have already made &quot;scenes&quot; where the players can find an shape the Clues?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That actually also bring up another problem I had: How do I guide my players in using it.<br /> <br /> I can imagen to some that being in that much charge can be overwhelming.. Or become a sort of power trip..<br /> <br /> ==============================<br /> <br /> ... I really would have liked the book to actually have some proper examples on how to do this -_-'</div> </div> </div> </div>I've heard that this subsystem was apparently heavily inspired by how GUMSHOE handles investigations, so maybe you could look there. Haven't read GUMSHOE myself, but it's a game *about* investigations. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T14:57:35-07:00","id":1134270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134087-investigations-clarification-contradiction?p=1134261#post1134261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would work great in some kind of a system where at end of the investigations, players accrue a certain number of Clue Points and then can trade them in to unlock options from a list provided by a GM.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of similar to how the CofD Investigation system works. The big difference is that instead of trading in Clue Elements for bonuses at the end, you get complications at the end for each Element you were short of a target number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-26T20:25:00-07:00","id":1134340,"title":"","content":"The way I read those sentences to mean &quot;What are you hoping to find and where? (so to make my job of coming up with a clue and their interpretation easier)&quot;<br /> <br /> Instead of making an ordeal out of gathering the evidence, complications should be about using what they've learned, from henchmen being sent to dissuade the PCs violently, to unpleasant political ramifications of the truth coming out of the box (Harvey Dent in Nolan's Dark Knight for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 08-26-2017, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-27T12:47:20-07:00","id":1134578,"title":"","content":"Never heard about GUMSHOE.. Maybe I'll give it a look and see if it can give some better examples.<br /> It is because I am planing on trying to run a semi-prepared setting so I have something to fall back on. Using the Junkyard story from Mysterious Places (from WoD) which already has allot of unanswered things in it, letting the ST make up his own things..<br /> <br /> But I am imagining that the later Clues, these points of interest, could change depending on what the players would &quot;find&quot; if I went with the free form/check point-like style. Like decide a dead body for the first, and depending on what they want to discover I could change the second Clue/point.<br /> <br /> What about elements? How do they tie into the Clue and using them? Is it where, as long as whatever they want to use the Element for is relevant to the Clue they can use it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6718-neros","name":"Neros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"137"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T04:12:03-07:00","id":1134800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1134087-investigations-clarification-contradiction?p=1134578#post1134578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about elements? How do they tie into the Clue and using them? Is it where, as long as whatever they want to use the Element for is relevant to the Clue they can use it?</div> </div> </div> </div>I run Clues and Elements this way - My players are looking for weird killer. One player decides to use his Science Skill on crime scene saying something like 'I look for the trail of the killer'. She rolls, get's a Clue - so she finds semi-hidden footprint, leading into North. If she would declare 'I look for the fibers', she would find some small piece on the bush, enought to make analyzying in lab. It's the Clue.<br /> <br /> Then for the Elements, I let players to use 'bonus' from found Clue to get next Clue. If using footprint as Clue, players can use Elements as bonus to pinpoint where are good hiding places for killer to find nearby. If using fiber as Clue, they can add Elements to rolls on Reaserch of fibers compositon or manufacturere. Basiclly, Elements are there to make chain reaction of Clues searching.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But if players use too much Elements, they can have complications in final resolution of Mystery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}